From a8db6a4f35a887f50f0c570de3df60c840474539 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Tue, 6 Oct 2026 15:23:53 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/3] lab(uefi): A.L.I.C.E. boot dashboard - GOP panels, live
 CIS-1 decode, attestation view

What a person at the machine sees is now a designed dashboard instead of a
white-on-black transcript: a header with the mark and a mode badge; MACHINE,
PAYLOAD and ATTESTATION panels filled from CPUID, file sizes, SHA-256s, TPM
PCRs, the TPM2_Quote result and the receipt digest/chain; a transcript
viewport that every existing print site writes into unchanged; and a footer
stage bar (BOOT..DONE).

- gop.rs: prefer the largest landscape mode <= 1920 px wide (QEMU std VGA
  otherwise offers a 2048x2048 square); viewport-relative newline/scroll;
  fill_rect, text_px, text_cell, set_viewport, clear_viewport primitives.
- console.rs: 1x glyphs unless the panel is >= 2560 px wide (120 columns at
  1920); with_gop() runs dashboard code only on the GOP backend.
- ui.rs (new): palette, layout, panels, header, footer, receipt lines.
- verifier.rs: replay_with(.., on_token), a display-only observer invoked
  after the chain fold; replay() wraps it with a no-op. Receipts are
  byte-identical with or without a screen: the RECEIPT.TXT minted under
  QEMU by this build equals tests/golden/witness_v1_m7_once64.receipt.
- main.rs: dashboard hooks at each stage; live token stream and token
  counter during mint; receipt summary in the attestation panel for mint
  and verify; a 3 s hold on the DONE frame before the test runner exits.

The firmware text-console fallback is unchanged (every ui:: call is a no-op
there). QEMU gate: mint and verify both exit 33 with swtpm attached; the
host verifier reports ATTEST VERIFY PASS and QUOTE VERIFY PASS for both
ATTEST.TXT files. No performance claims are made (Rule A).

